# 24-7BOT

A simple Minecraft AFK bot for Java Edition servers. It can stay connected, move around to avoid inactivity kicks, send occasional chat messages, reconnect automatically, and keep running for long periods.

This version is designed to be easier to understand, easier to configure, and easier to run on Termux or Linux.

## Features

- Auto-connect to a server
- Reconnect after disconnects or kicks
- AFK movement and jump loops
- Random chat messages to appear active
- Configurable timing through environment variables
- Friendly setup for beginners
- Cleaner, more maintainable code base

## Requirements

- Node.js 18 or newer
- Internet access
- A Minecraft Java Edition server
- A valid server IP and port

## Installation

### Linux

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y nodejs npm git

git clone https://github.com/ilhandv123/24-7BOT.git
cd 24-7BOT
npm install
```

### Termux (Android)

```bash
pkg update
pkg upgrade -y
pkg install -y nodejs git

git clone https://github.com/ilhandv123/24-7BOT.git
cd 24-7BOT
npm install
```

## Configuration

Copy the example file:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Then open `.env` and edit the values:

```env
MC_HOST=play.example.com
MC_PORT=25565
MC_USERNAME=ILHANBOT
MC_VERSION=1.21.11
RECONNECT_DELAY_MS=20000
CHAT_INTERVAL_MS=300000
JUMP_INTERVAL_MS=180000
MOVE_INTERVAL_MS=240000
RESTART_DELAY_MS=3600000
USERNAME_PREFIX=ILHANBOT
```

## Run the bot

```bash
npm start
```

If you do not want to use `.env`, you can also edit values directly in `bot.js` before running it.

## Important notes

- Use a valid server address and port.
- For Java Edition servers, use the server IP and port exactly as required by the server.
- Keep the bot name valid. It should not contain spaces if your server rejects them.
- Sometimes a server will kick a bot for suspicious activity. The bot will reconnect automatically.

## Troubleshooting

### The bot does not connect

- Check the server IP and port.
- Make sure the server is online.
- Confirm the server is Java Edition and not Bedrock.

### Bot gets kicked

- Check if the server has anti-cheat or anti-bot rules.
- Use a different username.
- Increase your reconnect delay if needed.

### Termux stops after some time

- Use a background process manager such as `nohup`, `screen`, or `tmux`.
- Example:

```bash
nohup npm start > bot.log 2>&1 &
```

## Beginner quick start

```bash
git clone https://github.com/ilhandv123/24-7BOT.git
cd 24-7BOT
npm install
cp .env.example .env
nano .env
npm start
```

